course: dictionary
lesson: 9710
title: Sultan
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A sultan is a king or ruler in some Muslim countries, both in history and today. Today there is the Sultan of Brunei and the Sultan of Oman.
explain: Look at the words around the word: «The Ottoman sultan Mehmed II captured Constantinople in 1453.» Captured tells you a sultan leads people and places. Ask: what word would fit here? A king or ruler fits, so that is the meaning.
explain: Sultan can also be part of a longer word or phrase. A country ruled by a sultan is a sultanate. Phrases to spot are «the Sultan of» and «sultan's palace».
explain: Being married to a sultan is not the same as being one. «Roksolana became the wife of Sultan Suleiman the Magnificent and had great influence at court, but she did not rule the empire.» The word but warns you of the difference.
fact: A sultan is a king or ruler in some Muslim countries.
fact: «Sultan Mehmed II» captured Constantinople in 1453, ending the Byzantine Empire.
fact: In history, the sultans of the Ottoman Empire ruled a huge empire from Istanbul.
fact: A country ruled by a sultan is called a sultanate.
fact: Sultans appear in stories like «One Thousand and One Nights».
exercise: «Babur defeated the Delhi Sultan at Panipat in 1526.» What is a sultan? | *A king or ruler in some Muslim countries | A fish that lives in rivers | A large boat with sails | A soldier who fights only on horseback
exercise: Which word means a country ruled by a sultan? | Sultry | *Sultanate | Sundial | Surgeon
exercise: Roksolana was the wife of a sultan. Did she rule the empire? | She ran away from the palace | *No, she had great influence at court but did not rule | Yes, she ruled the whole empire alone | She was a sultan too
test: In history, what did the Ottoman sultans rule from Istanbul? | A small village by the sea | A school for princes | A football club | *A huge empire
test: The Sultan of Brunei rules a country. What is that kind of country called? | *A sultanate | A village | A kingdom of islands with no ruler | A republic
exam: «Sultan Mehmed II captured Constantinople in 1453.» What was Mehmed II? | A captive from Rohatyn | A painter from Ukraine | A Cossack leader who wrote letters | *A ruler of the Ottoman Empire
